<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea Kia to sell auto parts to Poland Daewoo.</title>
<headline>S.Korea Kia to sell auto parts to Poland Daewoo.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kia Heavy Industries Co Ltd, a unit of South Korea's Kia Group, said on Tuesday it had agreed to export $50 million worth of transmissions to Daewoo Motor Poland Corp.</p>
<p>The transmissions would be used in small-sized Lublin trucks to be produced in the joint venture plant between Daewoo Motor Co Ltd of the Daewoo Group  and Fabryka Samochodow Lublin of Poland.</p>
<p>In 1995, Daewoo took over 67.8 percent of the Polish firm's capitalisation, valued at $80 million.</p>
<p>The flagship of the Kia Group is Kia Motors Corp.</p>
</text>
